---
import { SITE } from "@config/constants";
---

<div class="accessibility-experience">
  <header class="orientation scene grid">
    <h1>Accessibility</h1>
    <p class="framing">
      Teesside Digital wants this website to be usable by as many people as
      possible, including people who use a keyboard, screen magnification,
      high-contrast settings or assistive technology.
    </p>
    <p class="fact">Last reviewed: 13 October 2026</p>
  </header>
  <div class="statement scene">
    <section class="block grid" aria-labelledby="standard-heading">
      <h2 id="standard-heading">The standard</h2>
      <div class="block-body prose">
        <p>
          The target is WCAG 2.2 level AA, the widely used international
          standard for web accessibility.
        </p>
        <p>
          It is a target, not a certificate. The website has not been
          independently audited.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="block grid" aria-labelledby="checked-heading">
      <h2 id="checked-heading">What has been checked</h2>
      <div class="block-body prose">
        <p>These checks were carried out in Microsoft Edge on Windows:</p>
        <ul role="list">
          <li>
            using every page and both forms with a keyboard only, with a
            visible focus indicator throughout
          </li>
          <li>text enlarged to twice its normal size</li>
          <li>narrow screens down to 320 pixels wide</li>
          <li>high-contrast (forced colours) mode</li>
          <li>reduced-motion settings, which turn off the page animations</li>
          <li>with JavaScript turned off, including submitting both forms</li>
          <li>
            colour contrast of text, links and form controls in both the Dark
            and Light themes
          </li>
        </ul>
        <!-- UPDATE-AFTER-TEST: screen reader -->
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="block grid" aria-labelledby="unchecked-heading">
      <h2 id="unchecked-heading">Not yet checked</h2>
      <div class="block-body prose">
        <ul role="list">
          <li>other browsers, including Safari and Firefox</li>
          <li>real phones and tablets</li>
          <li>screen readers</li>
          <li>a full independent audit</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          These will be checked as the website develops, and this page will be
          updated.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="block grid" aria-labelledby="issues-heading">
      <h2 id="issues-heading">Known issues</h2>
      <div class="block-body prose">
        <p>
          On a very narrow screen with text enlarged to twice its normal size,
          some pages, including the home and services pages, become wider than
          the screen and need sideways scrolling. The Teesside Digital name at
          the top of the navigation can also run past the edge of the screen.
          These are due to be fixed.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="block grid" aria-labelledby="features-heading">
      <h2 id="features-heading">Features that help</h2>
      <div class="block-body prose">
        <ul role="list">
          <li>a "Skip to main content" link at the start of every page</li>
          <li>a choice of Dark or Light theme, remembered on your device</li>
          <li>
            animations are switched off if your device is set to reduce motion
          </li>
          <li>the website works without JavaScript, including both forms</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="block grid" aria-labelledby="report-heading">
      <h2 id="report-heading">Report a problem</h2>
      <div class="block-body prose">
        <p>
          If something on this website is difficult to use, or you need
          information from it in a different format, email
          <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          It helps to say which page you were on and what happened. Dave will
          reply by email and, where he can, provide the information another
          way.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  /* Privacy's sibling: the same container, grid, title scale, rules, lists and spacing. */
  .accessibility-experience {
    container: accessibility / inline-size;
    max-inline-size: 100rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
    color: rgb(var(--color-text));
  }
  .scene {
    margin-inline: 1.5rem;
    padding-block: 3rem 3.5rem;
  }
  .scene + .scene {
    border-block-start: var(--rule-width) solid rgb(var(--color-rule));
  }
  h1,
  h2,
  p,
  ul {
    margin: 0;
  }
  h1,
  h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 400;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 12cqi, 3.625rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.055em;
    line-height: 1;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.875rem, 8cqi, 2.25rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
  }
  p,
  li {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: rgb(var(--color-text-muted));
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
  }
  .grid > * {
    min-inline-size: 0;
  }
  .orientation {
    padding-block-start: 3.5rem;
  }
  .framing {
    margin-block-start: 2rem;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
    max-inline-size: 35ch;
  }
  .fact {
    margin-block-start: 3rem;
    border-block-start: var(--rule-width) solid rgb(var(--color-rule));
    padding-block-start: 1rem;
  }
  a {
    color: rgb(var(--color-action));
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  a:is(:hover, :focus-visible) {
    color: rgb(var(--color-action-hover));
  }
  /* Lead-ins are picked out by colour, not weight alone. */
  strong {
    font-weight: 500;
    color: rgb(var(--color-text));
  }
  /* The eight sections are separated by space alone. */
  .block + .block {
    margin-block-start: 3.5rem;
  }
  .block-body {
    margin-block-start: 1.5rem;
    max-inline-size: 65ch;
  }
  .prose > * + * {
    margin-block-start: 1.25rem;
  }
  ul {
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }
  /* A short dash in the text colour: the rule token is too faint in Light. */
  li {
    position: relative;
    padding-inline-start: 1.75rem;
  }
  li::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset-inline-start: 0;
    inset-block-start: 0.775em;
    inline-size: 0.875rem;
    border-block-start: var(--rule-width) solid currentColor;
  }
  li + li {
    margin-block-start: 0.5rem;
  }
  @container accessibility (min-width: 48rem) {
    .scene {
      margin-inline: 3rem;
      padding-block: 4rem 4.5rem;
    }
    .grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(12, minmax(0, 1fr));
      column-gap: 1.5rem;
    }
    p,
    li {
      font-size: 1.125rem;
    }
    h1 {
      font-size: clamp(5.5rem, 9cqi, 6.5rem);
    }
    h2 {
      font-size: clamp(2.375rem, 4cqi, 3rem);
    }
    .orientation {
      padding-block: 4rem 3.5rem;
    }
    .orientation h1 {
      grid-column: 1 / 6;
      grid-row: 1;
    }
    .framing {
      grid-column: 7 / 12;
      grid-row: 1;
      margin-block-start: 4.5rem;
      font-size: 1.375rem;
    }
    .fact {
      grid-column: 1 / 6;
      grid-row: 2;
      font-size: 1rem;
      margin-block-start: 3.5rem;
    }
    .block + .block {
      margin-block-start: 5rem;
    }
    .block h2 {
      grid-column: 1 / 4;
      grid-row: 1;
    }
    .block-body {
      grid-column: 5 / 12;
      grid-row: 1;
      margin-block-start: 0.5rem;
    }
  }
  /* "Accessibility" is one long word: it takes a sixth column and scales to stay on one line. */
  @container accessibility (min-width: 48rem) {
    .orientation h1 {
      grid-column: 1 / 7;
      font-size: min(
        clamp(5.5rem, 9cqi, 6.5rem),
        calc((50cqi - 3.75rem) / 5.3)
      );
    }
  }
  @media (forced-colors: active) {
    a {
      color: LinkText;
    }
    strong {
      color: CanvasText;
    }
    .scene + .scene,
    .fact {
      border-color: CanvasText;
    }
  }
</style>
